UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Notion AI is the assistant built into the Notion workspace. Its October 2026 updates turned it into an agent system that connects to outside AI assistants via MCP, syncs Skills through a Skills API, draws on models from several AI vendors, and now includes Notion Agents with their own computer and browser for tasks lasting up to 24 hours.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'notion-ai' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Notion AI is the artificial-intelligence layer inside Notion, the document and database workspace. It lives directly in your pages, so instead of switching to a separate chatbot you summon it where your notes, wikis and project databases already are.

The latest numbered release is Notion 3.8, shipped October 13, 2026, under the theme 'Context for your agents'. It lets outside AI agents connect into a workspace through MCP with admin controls, adds a Skills API that syncs Skills written in Notion out to assistants such as ChatGPT and Claude, and brings in new models from vendors including OpenAI and Anthropic. On October 19, 2026 Notion shipped a further, unnumbered update, 'Agents, rebuilt to do more for less', which introduced a single AI credit system covering the Notion Agent, Custom Agents and connected outside tools, an upgraded Auto model router that Notion says matches top-tier model quality on common tasks at a fraction of the credit cost, Notion Agents that get their own computer and browser and can run for up to 24 hours, a 'Review for me' mode, the ability to connect a ChatGPT Plus, Pro or Go account to a user's personal Notion Agent (not yet Custom Agents), and a private alpha of bring-your-own-key for Enterprise. The new credit system is live for new customers now and rolls out to existing customers on November 2, 2026.

Earlier, the 3.7 release (September 2026) had added an agent Skills system with a skills library, the ability to export Skills to external tools such as Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini and Grok, Custom Agents that can call sub-agents, a Notion Agents iOS app, and a redesigned model picker. The 3.6 release before that (July 2026) introduced orchestration of External Agents such as Claude and Cursor from shared boards, AI-generated interactive HTML blocks, reading and writing Microsoft Office files (PPTX, XLSX, DOCX) and Outlook, AI Meeting Notes with speaker identification, Enterprise Search across connected apps, and a Research Mode.

Day to day the AI can draft and rewrite text, translate, summarize long pages, fill and query databases, answer questions across your whole workspace, and run multi-step agent tasks. Under the new credit system, each Business and Enterprise seat includes 1,500 Standard credits a month, used when Notion's Auto router picks the model, and 500 Select credits a month, used when you pick the model yourself or run Custom Agents you build. Workspace admins can buy additional credits for the whole workspace; Notion's pricing page still lists this at $10 per 1,000 monthly Notion credits. Custom Agent activity can be tracked through audit logging on higher plans.

Pricing has four tiers, listed per seat per month on notion.com/pricing, with up to 20% off for yearly billing. Free is $0 per seat per month but only includes a capped trial of Notion AI, not ongoing access. Plus is $10 per seat per month and also only includes the AI trial. Business is $20 per seat per month and is the cheapest plan with full, ongoing AI, including the Notion Agent, AI Meeting Notes, Enterprise Search, and the new monthly credit allotment. Enterprise is custom-priced and adds a private alpha of bring-your-own-key plus zero data retention with LLM providers. Notion AI is not sold as a separate add-on; it is bundled into the Business and Enterprise seat price, with extra purchased credits as a variable cost on top. A user's personal Notion Agent can also be connected to a ChatGPT Plus, Pro or Go account to help cover its usage, though this does not yet extend to Custom Agents.

The main catch is that ongoing AI access sits behind the Business plan: Free and Plus users only get a capped AI trial, so casual users who expect free or cheap AI on their existing workspace will hit a wall quickly. Even on Business and Enterprise, heavy AI or Custom Agent use can exceed the included Standard and Select credits, requiring admins to buy more at an added, usage-based cost, and some higher-end features such as audit logging and bring-your-own-key remain reserved for upper tiers or in alpha. Notion AI makes most sense for teams already running their knowledge base, docs and projects in Notion who want AI in the same place and are on or willing to move to the Business tier; solo note-takers on the Free or Plus plan will find the AI too limited to rely on day to day.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'notion-ai' AND lang = 'en';

