UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Perplexity is an AI-powered answer engine that returns cited, up-to-date sources instead of a list of links, with an agentic Deep Research mode and multi-model access to systems from OpenAI, Anthropic, Google and other vendors.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'perplexity' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Perplexity is a conversational search tool that answers questions with cited, up-to-date sources instead of a list of links. It sits somewhere between a chatbot and a search engine, and it has leaned hard into research and agentic work.

As of October 2026, Perplexity's Computer assistant can run fully locally on Apple-silicon Macs, with 36GB or more of RAM recommended. In local mode the model, orchestration harness, and task execution all stay on-device; it can touch local files and apps such as Notes, Messages, Mail and Numbers only with the user's permission, runs code and tools in sandboxes, and can escalate to more than 15 cloud frontier models only if the user authorizes it. Local mode uses local models including one from Qwen and a Perplexity-trained model called PPLX Pro, and is available to Pro, Max and Enterprise subscribers, giving them more control over credit spend.

The other headline feature is Advanced Deep Research. It runs agentically inside Perplexity's Computer assistant, asks clarifying questions before it starts, accepts follow-ups mid-run, and shows live source and progress tracking.

Beyond research, Perplexity gives you multi-model access to systems from OpenAI, Anthropic, Google and other vendors, plus the Comet browser for AI-assisted browsing.

Pricing is tiered. Free costs $0 a month. Pro costs $20 a month or $200 a year billed annually, shown by Perplexity as a $17-a-month equivalent, and includes 4,000 bonus Computer credits. Max costs $200 a month or $2,000 a year billed annually, shown as a $167-a-month equivalent, and includes 10,000 monthly Computer credits plus 35,000 bonus credits.

The limitations are worth knowing. Like any AI system it can still misread or over-trust weak sources, so citations need checking. The free tier is limited for frequent use, agentic Computer work is metered by a monthly credit budget that heavy users can exhaust, and fully local Computer mode is restricted to Apple-silicon Macs with substantial RAM. Juggling multiple models also adds a learning curve for some users. Perplexity suits people who do a lot of source-backed research, want agentic Deep Research, or like having several AI models in one subscription, while casual users who need only a few answers a day can stay on the free tier.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'perplexity' AND lang = 'en';

