UPDATE tools SET description = $x$ElevenLabs is a multimodal AI studio on a single credit balance: speech, voice cloning, music, sound effects, transcription, dubbing, and image and video generation with lip sync. It runs its own Eleven v4 and Eleven v4 Turbo voice models and aggregates third-party models from ByteDance, Google, OpenAI, Black Forest Labs and others, so one subscription covers most media formats.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'elevenlabs' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$ElevenLabs is a voice-focused AI company best known for realistic text-to-speech and voice cloning. Beyond TTS it now spans audiobooks, music generation and voice agents, making it one of the more complete audio stacks available to developers and creators.

The flagship text-to-speech models are Eleven v4 and Eleven v4 Turbo, released September 28, 2026, supporting more than 90 languages across ElevenAgents, ElevenCreative and the ElevenAPI; v4 Turbo is the low-latency variant built for voice agents, with around 100ms median inference latency and roughly 150ms median time to first speech over WebSocket. The earlier Eleven v3, which reached general availability in February 2026, remains available but has been superseded by v4 for most use cases. On October 20, 2026, ElevenLabs added Eleven Realtime, a pair of dedicated speech-to-speech voice-agent models: Eleven Realtime v1 Mini, the default choice for lowest latency and cost, and v1 Max, which reasons before responding. Both are OpenAI Realtime API-compatible, WebSocket-only, available through ElevenAgents or a standalone Realtime API, and support more than 90 languages plus a library of over 17,000 voices. Vendor benchmarks put time to first audio at about 0.57 seconds for Max and 0.62 seconds for Mini, with Big Bench Audio scores of 98.8% and 75.9% respectively.

Core capabilities include high-quality multilingual TTS, instant voice cloning from about 10 seconds of audio, professional studio-grade cloning, real-time conversational agents built on Eleven Realtime or Eleven v4 Turbo, music generation, and an API with its own subscription tiers for production use. Mini is not available under Zero Retention Mode or HIPAA compliance, and Max is not offered with India or Singapore data residency.

There is a free plan with 10,000 credits per month and no commercial license, covering TTS, speech-to-text, sound effects, voice design, music and image generation. Paid tiers are billed monthly or annually (annual billing gives two months free): Starter is $6/mo ($5/mo billed annually, 30,000 credits), currently discounted to $1 for the first month until November 1; Creator is $22/mo ($18.33/mo billed annually, 121,000 credits), with a promotional $11 first month; Pro is $99/mo ($82.50/mo billed annually, 600,000 credits); Scale is $299/mo ($249.17/mo billed annually, 1.8M credits, 3 seats); and Business is $990/mo ($825/mo billed annually, 6M credits, 10 seats). Custom Enterprise pricing is also available. The separate Eleven Realtime API is billed at $0.080 per minute of connected audio for both models (burst rate $0.160/min above your concurrency limit), plus token costs of $0.20 per 1M input and $6.00 per 1M output tokens for Mini, or $1.80 per 1M input and $9.00 per 1M output for Max.

The main limitations are credit-based usage that can run out quickly on higher-volume work, no commercial rights on the free plan, and costs that climb fast once you need many hours of audio or several seats. Promotional first-month pricing on Starter and Creator reverts to the standard monthly rate afterward, and voice cloning raises consent and misuse concerns you have to manage yourself.

ElevenLabs suits creators, studios and developers who need natural-sounding voices in many languages, teams building voice agents, and anyone producing audiobooks or narration at scale.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'elevenlabs' AND lang = 'en';

