UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Zapier is a workflow automation platform connecting 9,000+ apps, with Zapier Copilot building automations from plain language, AI by Zapier running AI-driven steps inside Zaps, and Zapier MCP exposing Zapier's actions to external LLMs such as Claude and ChatGPT.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'zapier-ai' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Zapier is a cloud automation service that connects the apps you already use, moving data and tasks between them without manual copy-paste. You build workflows called Zaps that run on triggers and actions, and the same account also offers Tables, Interfaces, and Chatbots.

As of October 2026, Zapier folded its standalone Zapier Agents product into a new feature called AI by Zapier: agent-style automation now lives inside a Zap as an AI step with a prompt field, a tools picker, and per-tool approval, triggered like any other Zap and run on a choice of model tiers (Standard, Advanced, Premium) or a named model. Standalone Agents built in the old product are being migrated to this step-based format; Zapier has not announced a shutdown date for the legacy Agents experience and says it will notify users by email.

Alongside AI by Zapier, Zapier Copilot (in Beta on every plan) builds and edits Zaps, Tables, Interfaces, Chatbots, and agent steps from plain-language descriptions. Zapier MCP exposes Zapier's triggers and actions to external large language models such as Claude and ChatGPT, with each MCP tool call drawing from the plan's task quota. Core integration coverage stands at 9,000+ apps, with multi-step Zaps, filters, paths, formatting, and webhooks available throughout.

Zapier's core plans are Free ($0/month, 100 tasks/month, unlimited two-step Zaps, Tables, and Forms), Professional (from $19.99/month billed annually, or $29.99/month billed monthly, starting at 750 tasks and scaling to 2 million), Team (from $69/month billed annually, or $103.50/month billed monthly, for 25 users starting at 2,000 tasks), and custom-priced Enterprise. AI by Zapier is included on Professional, Team, and Enterprise plans, not on Free, and bills out of the same task pool: steps using Zapier's default models are free, while other model tiers cost a multiplier of 1, 3, or 5 tasks per run, with runs capped at 75 tasks by default (admins can raise this to 500). A separate Chatbots add-on remains on the pricing page (a free tier with 2 bots, a Pro tier around $13.33/month billed annually, and an Advanced tier around $66.67/month billed annually), and the legacy stand-alone Agents add-on (a free tier with 400 activities/month and a Pro tier around $33.33/month billed annually) is still listed but is being phased out as Agents migrates into AI by Zapier.

The main limitation is cost at scale: tasks meter everything, and AI steps on non-default models consume extra tasks quickly. Advanced logic can get fiddly, and the newly reorganized AI by Zapier steps still benefit from per-tool human approval before you let them run unattended, especially during the migration period while legacy Agents are moved over.

Zapier fits teams and solo operators who want to automate across many SaaS tools without code and who want AI to draft, run, and maintain those automations from inside the same Zap editor. If you need only one or two heavy, high-volume pipelines, a cheaper task model elsewhere may serve you better.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'zapier-ai' AND lang = 'en';

