UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Replit Agent 4 runs parallel agents that build authentication, database, backend, and frontend components simultaneously, and includes a Security Agent that scans codebases for vulnerabilities. A newer Monitoring Agent can investigate production issues from app logs and metrics and attempt validated fixes.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'replit' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Replit is a browser-based development platform that combines a cloud IDE, AI coding agent, and instant deployment into a single environment. No local setup is required — users write, run, and ship code entirely in the browser, making it accessible for beginners and fast for prototyping.

The current generation, Agent 4, repositions Replit from an AI coding agent toward a broader creative agent, described by Replit as turning ideas into apps, designs, slides, and more, with design variants generated on an infinite canvas as a headline feature. A newer Monitoring Agent, introduced in October 2026, investigates production issues using app logs and metrics, then attempts and validates fixes; users can enable Monitoring alerts and an opt-in Auto-fix feature for background triage, while an experimental Auto-republish option can publish validated fixes automatically. Otherwise, fixes are reviewed and published by the user.

Agent 4 introduces multi-task parallelism: instead of building an app sequentially, it spins up parallel agents that handle authentication, database setup, backend logic, and frontend code at the same time, with progress visible in a dedicated panel. The Security Agent performs codebase scanning at three levels: a free dependency and static code analysis pass, a white-box scan, and a combined white-box plus black-box scan; Replit has not published scan duration figures. Higher-tier Power and Max modes let users manually select a model from third-party providers including OpenAI and Anthropic, while Free Mode always uses automatic intelligent model routing. The Agent can also create and update workspace skills, supports chat and asset sharing, and offers a discounted Stripe Atlas incorporation service.

Pricing, read from replit.com/pricing, has no listed $0 account tier. Core costs $20/month billed monthly, or $18/month billed annually, and includes $20 in monthly credits plus a Free Mode allowance of up to 30 hours of chat and 60 projects. Pro costs $100/month billed monthly, or $90/month billed annually, includes $100 in credits, 10 parallel agents, up to 15 collaborators and 50 viewers, and 28-day database rollback. Enterprise pricing is custom and adds SSO, SCIM and audit logs, advanced privacy controls, centralized security, and single-tenant and private networking options.

Free Mode, included inside the paid tiers, resets its usage allowance every 5 hours and always uses automatic intelligent model routing rather than manual model selection, which is reserved for Power and Max modes. Generated code across all tiers often needs review before production use, and the browser-based environment can feel slower than local editors for large projects.

Replit suits developers who want to go from idea to deployed app quickly, students learning full-stack development, and small teams that need built-in collaboration and automated security scanning without managing their own infrastructure, provided they are willing to pay for a Core or Pro plan since no free account tier is currently offered.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'replit' AND lang = 'en';

