UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Anthropic's AI assistant, known for careful reasoning, coding, and long documents. Current models include Claude Fable 5.1 (most capable, widely released), Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, and Claude Haiku 5.5, plus the limited-availability Claude Mythos 5.1. Free plan plus Pro ($20/mo billed monthly, or $17/mo billed annually), Max, Team, and Enterprise plans.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'claude' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Claude is a conversational AI assistant from Anthropic, used through the web app, mobile apps, and the API. It handles long-form writing, analysis, coding, document reading, and multi-step reasoning, with an emphasis on careful, steerable responses.

As of October 2026, the model lineup is unchanged: Claude Fable 5.1 (the most capable widely released model), Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, and Claude Haiku 5.5 (released October 7, 2026, the first Haiku model with adjustable effort and now the default Haiku model in Claude Code), plus the limited-availability Claude Mythos 5.1 through the invitation-only Cyber Verification Program. Anthropic has also introduced Claude Duet, a standalone proactive-agent app for iOS, Android, and claude.ai, currently in research preview for US Pro and Max subscribers via waitlist; it runs on Opus 5.5 and uses the subscriber's existing plan limits at no extra cost, and is not yet available on Team or Enterprise plans. For Enterprise customers, Anthropic has merged the chat and Cowork experiences into a single unified Claude interface, generally available since October 23, 2026 (off by default for existing organizations until it becomes the default on November 16, 2026; not available for ZDR, HIPAA, or CMEK organizations).

All four current models, Fable 5.1, Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5, and Haiku 5.5, support a 1M-token context window, which helps with large codebases, long documents, or full transcripts in one conversation. The models also support multimodal input and tool use across the product. Opus 5.5 gained a fast mode that left research preview on the API on October 15, 2026, and became available on Google Cloud on October 22, 2026, running at roughly double the price for up to 2.5x faster responses.

Pricing is tiered. The Free plan is $0 and includes access to Sonnet and Haiku models, with usage caps. Pro is $20/month billed monthly, or $17/month if billed annually, and covers Opus, Sonnet, and Haiku plus Claude Code, with Fable 5.1 available through usage credits. Max starts from $100/month across 5x and 20x usage tiers and includes $100-$200/month in API credits; pricing above the $100 entry tier is not published. Team offers a Standard seat at $25/month billed monthly ($20/month billed annually) and a Premium seat at $125/month billed monthly ($100/month billed annually), for 2 to 150 users, with up to $500/month in pooled API credits. Enterprise costs $20/seat/month billed annually plus usage billed at API rates, with a 20-seat minimum. API list pricing per million tokens is $10/$50 for Fable 5.1, $4/$20 for Opus 5.5 (fast mode $8/$40), $2/$10 for Sonnet 5.5, and $0.10/$0.50 for Haiku 5.5 (prompts over 100K tokens: $0.50/$2.50).

Limitations are worth noting. Free and paid plans carry usage caps that reset on a rolling basis, so heavy users can hit limits mid-session. Max pricing beyond the $100/month entry tier isn't publicly disclosed, and the top-end Mythos 5.1 is invitation-only and not generally available. Opus 5.5 fast mode isn't available on the Batch API and is usage-credit only within Claude Code subscriptions. Enterprise requires a 20-seat minimum, which raises the entry cost for smaller organizations. As with any LLM, outputs still need checking for factual accuracy.

Claude suits writers, developers, analysts, and teams who want strong reasoning, large-context handling across its current model lineup, and a choice of models and plans, including the new proactive Duet agent for subscribers who want hands-off task assistance.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'claude' AND lang = 'en';

