 WHERE slug = 'deepseek' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$DeepSeek is a conversational AI assistant from the Chinese lab of the same name. It offers a web chat interface at chat.deepseek.com alongside a metered API that developers can build on. It handles general chat, coding, reasoning, and long-document work.

The API currently serves two model families: deepseek-flash, now served by the DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 model released October 17, 2026, and deepseek-v4-pro, running DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813. Older model names such as deepseek-chat and deepseek-reasoner no longer appear on the pricing page; legacy aliases deepseek-v4-flash and deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp are still accepted, but the underlying models are retired and requests are now served by DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 at the deepseek-flash price. The V4.1-Flash-1017 update brings better benchmark results, faster task completion, shorter outputs, and reinforcement learning with self-feedback for end-to-end project development, and is optimized for DeepSeek Harness (v0.2.1-rc.1 and later), Tencent CodeBuddy, and WorkBuddy.

Both models offer a 1M-token context window with output up to 384K tokens, and a default thinking mode with selectable low, high, and max reasoning effort. Vision input is supported on deepseek-flash but not on deepseek-v4-pro. Model weights for the deepseek-flash family are published on Hugging Face and ModelScope under an MIT license, with 763 billion parameters. DeepSeek documents agent integrations including Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, and its own DeepSeek Harness, and has added standalone Search and Fetch APIs.

API pricing is billed per 1 million tokens and varies by peak and off-peak UTC hours, with off-peak priced at half the peak rate. Peak hours are 01:00-04:00 and 06:00-10:00 UTC, Monday to Friday, excluding Chinese public holidays. For deepseek-flash: input on a cache miss is $0.15 off-peak / $0.30 peak, input on a cache hit is $0.003 off-peak / $0.006 peak, and output is $0.60 off-peak / $1.20 peak. For deepseek-v4-pro: input on a cache miss is $0.66 off-peak / $1.32 peak, input on a cache hit is $0.022 off-peak / $0.044 peak, and output is $1.98 off-peak / $3.96 peak. The new Search and Fetch APIs cost $0.75 per 1,000 successful requests each, though calls routed through DeepSeek Harness, Claude Code, or Codex are free of charge until November 1, 2026 at 00:00 Beijing time (October 31, 2026, 16:00 UTC). The pricing page also references a 'granted balance' used before any topped-up balance, but does not explain how or when it is granted. Pricing for the web chat interface could not be confirmed on a primary page at time of writing.

Limitations to keep in mind: whether the web chat remains free could not be re-verified today, the 'granted balance' mechanism is unclear, concurrency is capped at 2,500 requests for deepseek-flash and 500 for deepseek-v4-pro, vision is Flash-only, the model lineup has changed several times in recent months, and as a China-based service it may raise data-residency or compliance questions for some organizations.

DeepSeek suits developers who want a low-cost, long-context API for coding, reasoning, or high-volume tasks, who may want to self-host the open-weight deepseek-flash model, and who are comfortable tracking peak/off-peak pricing and occasional model migrations.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'deepseek' AND lang = 'en';

