UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Lovable is an agentic no-code platform that turns plain-language prompts into working web apps. It builds autonomously through a default Agent/Build mode, with Plan Mode for previewing changes and automatic subagents handling parallel research and review work, all metered by a unified credit system.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'lovable' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Lovable lets you describe an app in everyday language and have it built for you, including the interface, logic, and a managed backend. It is aimed at founders, product people, and developers who want to go from idea to a deployable app without writing everything by hand.

The product runs on a fully agentic, credit-based model rather than a versioned release cycle. Agent Mode (also called Build mode) is the default and runs autonomously: it reads your codebase, searches the web, debugs, generates images, and validates its own output. Plan Mode lets you preview intended changes before any code is written, now with diffs and revision history, and Lovable also runs automatic, read-only subagents that handle research and review work in parallel. As of late 2026, builds can run for extended periods per message under a '/goal' mode, and in-app AI features can use Anthropic's Claude models without you supplying your own API key.

On capabilities, the backend is branded Lovable Cloud, a managed layer built on Supabase under the hood, with Lovable AI handling in-app AI features. You get database, auth, and hosting without wiring raw services yourself. Workspace-private projects are included even on the free plan.

Pricing is credit-based across both building and running apps. Free is $0 with 5 build credits per day (capped at about 30 per month), plus a shared monthly allowance of 20 Cloud credits, 4 in-app AI credits, and 1 connector credit that Lovable also extends to paid tiers. Pro costs $25/mo billed monthly, or $21/mo billed annually, for a 100-credit plan, and adds credit rollovers, top-ups, custom domains, user roles, and badge removal. Business costs $50/mo billed monthly, or $42/mo billed annually, for a 100-credit plan, and adds team workspace features, role-based access, workspace publishing, SSO, and a security center. Enterprise pricing is a custom platform fee plus volume pricing, with SCIM, audit logs, and EU inference options.

The main limitation is the credit model itself: because credits cover building, deployed-app runtime, and in-app AI, costs can be hard to predict on active projects, and the free tier runs out quickly. Lovable also describes the monthly Cloud, AI, and connector credit grants, along with the current per-message chat pricing, as temporary arrangements subject to change. Autonomous generation is fast but still needs review, and heavy customization eventually pushes you into editing code directly.

Choose Lovable if you want an AI agent to do most of the building and you are comfortable steering it, and budget for credit consumption if your app is more than a prototype.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'lovable' AND lang = 'en';

